 [:a {:href "/athletes/1202561"} "John Cuthbert Moore"] ", 1st Baron Brabazon of Tara, was also highly considered, but fell off his sled at the Shuttlecock curve only 2 days before the Olympic event started, broke several ribs, and cut his face badly.  He did not start."] "\n\n" [:p {} "With Northesk behind, the two American Heaton brothers could decide the title between them, with " [:a {:href "/athletes/86530"} "Jennison"] " eventually taking the gold and  " [:a {:href "/athletes/86531"} "Jack"] " the silver. Jack Heaton did quite well when one considers he was hampered by a broken wrist he had sustained only a few weeks before the Olympic race. Two of the ten competitors crashed, as the Frenchman " [:a {:href "/athletes/85267"} "Pierre Dormeuil"] " and Swiss " [:a {:href "/athletes/98710"} "Willy Voneschen"] " both left the course involuntarily."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {} "Run #1"] [:th {} "Run #2"] [:th {} "Run #3"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/86530"} "Jennison Heaton"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "3:01.8"] [:td {} "1:00.2 (1)"] [:td {} "1:00.2 (1)"] [:td {} "1:01.4 (=2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/86531"} "Jack Heaton"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "3:02.8"] [:td {} "1:01.4 (2)"] [:td {} "1:00.4 (2)"] [:td {} "1:01.0 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/959